{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "כבד את אביך ואת אמך", :translit "kabed et avikha ve-et imekha", :gloss "Honor your father and your mother"} {:he "סמך כבוד אב ואם לשבת", :translit "samakh kevod av ve-em le-shabat", :gloss "He juxtaposed honor of father and mother to Sabbath"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Juxtaposition (semikhut) of the mitzvah of honoring parents to the commandment of Sabbath in the verse sequence"}], :frame {:text "The principle that verbal juxtaposition in the Torah generates legal inference is a standard hermeneutical method (Berakhot 2a, Pesahim 21b). The specific comparison drawn here equates honoring parents with honoring the Sabbath.", :sources ["Berakhot 2a" "Pesahim 21b"]}} {:quotes [{:he "למען יארכון", :translit "le-ma'an ya'arikhun", :gloss "so that they lengthen (your days)"} {:he "שאין אריכות ימים בעוה\"ז שנברא בה'", :translit "she-ein arikhut yamim ba-olam ha-zeh she-nivra be-hei", :gloss "for length of days is not in this world which was created with hei"} {:he "אלא בעוה\"ב שנברא ביו\"ד", :translit "ela ba-olam ha-ba she-nivra be-yod", :gloss "but in the World to Come which was created with yod"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Defective spelling of יארכון lacking yod signals that 'length of days' refers to the World to Come, created with the letter yod, not this world created with hei"} {:kind :other, :note "This world was created with the letter ה (hei); the World to Come with י (yod), based on Isaiah 26:4 read as 'for in Y-H He formed worlds'"}], :frame {:text "Isaiah 26:4 reads 'כִּי בְיָה־יְהוָה צוּר עוֹלָמִים' ('for in Yah the LORD formed worlds'), which is read as: with the two letters yod and hei, God formed two worlds. Menahot 29b states this world was created with hei and the World to Come with yod. The defective spelling of יארכון, missing its yod, teaches that the promised 'length of days' belongs not to this world but to the World to Come.", :sources ["Isaiah 26:4" "Menahot 29b"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Juxtaposition (semikhut) of the mitzvah of honoring parents to the commandment of Sabbath in the verse sequence", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :other, :note "Defective spelling of יארכון lacking yod signals that 'length of days' refers to the World to Come, created with the letter yod, not this world created with hei", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :other, :note "This world was created with the letter ה (hei); the World to Come with י (yod), based on Isaiah 26:4 read as 'for in Y-H He formed worlds'", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:17:41.093101933Z", :model "glm-5.2"}